0,Maʼdi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maʼdi_language,"Maʼdi (pronounced [màɗɨ́]) is a Central Sudanic language spoken in Uganda and South Sudan. It is one of the Moru-Madi languages. The Madi people refer to their language as Maʼdi ti, literally ""Ma ʼ di mouth"". The Ma ʼ di people are found in Magwi County in South Sudan, and in Adjumani and Moyo districts in Uganda. Their population is about 390,000 (90,000 in South Sudan). Ma ʼ di is ...","Ma’di, Southern",Nilo-Saharan
1,Sub-Saharan African music traditions - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-Saharan_African_music_traditions,"In many parts of sub-Saharan Africa, the use of music is not limited to entertainment: it serves a purpose to the local community and helps in the conduct of daily routines. Traditional African music supplies appropriate music and dance for work and for religious ceremonies of birth, naming, rites of passage, marriage and funerals. [1]","Ma’di, Southern",Nilo-Saharan
