6,Ma'di bowl lyre music and dance - UNESCO - Intangible Heritage Home,https://ich.unesco.org/en/USL/ma-di-bowl-lyre-music-and-dance-01187,"The Ma'di bowl lyre music and dance is a cultural practice of the Madi people of Uganda. Passed on by the community's ancestors, the songs and dances involved in the tradition are performed for various purposes, including weddings, political rallies, to celebrate good harvests, educate children, resolve conflict or mourn the passing of loved ones. Several rituals also take place regarding ...","Ma’di, Southern",Nilo-Saharan
